{
  "text": "Sam, thank you for sitting down with me today. It is an honor to be here. Let us jump right into artificial general intelligence. When people look at language models, they miss the critical safety question. The real immediate danger is targeted persuasion that feels completely human. Everyone worries about superhuman robots taking over tomorrow. Imagine millions of synthetic personas influencing elections and societal trust. We are not prepared for cognitive persuasion at this scale. We need robust watermarking and open public safety audits right now. That keeps me up at night far more than science fiction scenarios. Society must adapt in lockstep with the models. Why Fast Takeoff Is Dangerous. We need society to co-evolve with the technology, not wake up to a god in a datacenter. Iterative deployment allows institutions to adapt and fix bugs gradually. If you hold an intelligence explosion in secret, nobody knows how to govern it. Public access and feedback is our safest alignment strategy. The wisdom of humanity collective is smarter than any single lab.",
